            "contentType": "STORY",
            "title": "Investors Turn to Derivatives for US Corporate Bonds As Issuers Can't Keep Up",
            "description": "",
            "summary": "Blue-chip businesses have sold more than $1 trillion of bonds this year through August, data compiled by Bloomberg shows.  Without enough new notes to buy, money managers are turning to the credit derivatives market to make up the difference, gaining exposure to more than $110 billion of debt through the main North American high-grade credit-default swap index, according to DTCC data compiled by Barclays Plc.  \u201cThe money keeps coming in, and it needs to be invested,\u201d said Travis King, head of US investment-grade corporates at Voya Investment Management.",
